KZ3 patch 4020 (RSX pass 98): raw mouse input counts as keyboard+mouse activity for the button prompts.
Hand play 2026-10-22: with only the mouse in use the prompts stayed on the pad glyphs, because cellPad.c's s_keys_active
(patch 4011, pad_prompt_track) came only from the keyboard state. libs/input/pad_mouse.{h,c}: PadMouseAct (pure) =
a mouse button down or wheel step is activity at once; motion counts when |dx|+|dy| reaches PAD_MOUSE_ACT_COUNTS (8)
inside one PAD_MOUSE_ACT_WINDOW_MS (100 ms) window, so a bumped desk leaves the prompts alone. pad_mouse.c's WM_INPUT
feeds every raw mouse report in (buttons from usButtonFlags, motion for relative reports only) and
pad_mouse_activity_take() hands it to cellPad.c once per poll. The pad and keyboard rules are unchanged (a pad with
input in the same poll still wins). Needs the raw input registration of mouse look (KZ3_MOUSE_LOOK=0: no activity).
Host test tools/smoke/test_mouse_act.sh.
Also a bounded diagnostic for the Wine Wayland question (RSX pass 98): "[mouse] raw stats: N relative report(s) in S s:
C counts, max M in one report, A counts/report" per motion burst (first 30 lines), so a hand log shows what the driver
delivers per report (compare PROTON_ENABLE_WAYLAND=1 with the default driver over the same physical mouse move).

